Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary input to its Binary-Coded Decimal (BCD) representation. The module uses lookup tables to first translate the binary value to its decimal equivalent, and then to convert that decimal value into its corresponding BCD format, effectively allowing the input binary values ranging from 0 to 9 to be represented in a BCD form, where only the most significant digits are utilized.
