Implement the Verilog module based on the following description.
Design a 12-bit parallel-to-serial shift register with synchronous load. The register shifts data out one bit at a time on each clock cycle when the enable signal is high. The register loads parallel data when the load signal is high.

// Signals are defined as below:
// (1) load: Loads the register with data[11:0] instead of shifting. Active high.
// (2) ena: Enables the shifting of data. Active high.
// (3) data: The 12-bit parallel data input to be loaded.
// (4) q: The serial output of the register.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input load,
    input ena,
    input [11:0] data,
    output reg q);

